 saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.887,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-6-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7006012","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c8bb449b78421d454f7d3dbe983cb8cdafffae87d64f6ecae2c2ec1d68f131f1","compact":"9a8761bfdfc3ab7db3faba28ff7789636bb54849f59abd9be935af0c4d7a1971","nasal":"d219c11e1a8732f3041d73285f6901e2a435ef623e59d7bee311b77a77e9823c"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-6-13","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":6,"verse":13,"english":"O god, by virtue of the boon (that has been bestowed on them), resembling the three fires, Sukesa's three sons, assailing us, have deprived us of our abode.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.891,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-6-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7006013","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8c35c80b3ae51dc2bb08f6d651efc91601b62314bd1d9a8e2c441c160cc9ae6d","compact":"8ba24c31fa2ac204f9b50f6a7546770a5b2523e277de4486e4ca3f81dce5fca1","nasal":"8ba24c31fa2ac204f9b50f6a7546770a5b2523e277de4486e4ca3f81dce5fca1"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-6-14","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":6,"verse":14,"english":"There is a city named Lankā, stationed on the top of Trikuta, (extremely) difficult of entrance. Taking up their station at that place, the nightrangers in a body pursue us.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-6-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7006014","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"52b47468e377be6ec69fdd1ea1b377870101831ab04b8181589c748f26aa5adf","compact":"c60a5a3e84ad3e8d5447214547524d137cc8e4cc902275048fed4336174fef40","nasal":"91011619f3d8af0697582950402e61aecb53fe81ac2c8d5289f2e8ea9158818a"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-6-15","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":6,"verse":15,"english":"Do you dedicate to Yama the lotuses of their faces, severed (in pieces) with your discus. Save you, we have none who can, while tormented with fright, inspire us with courage.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.233,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-6-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7006015","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ca88ef584d5954975754e7c5d628cb309e2dc4afe8ff940b42db3944dc30b0cd","compact":"ed0b90656d483b830e44f4b73396f0c5ca31d4da61fb62b0c6171438d6d17fbd","nasal":"d75f948e3d9b262955d2230707f0b6cbc65ecd0e4c7fcd162cceca9987e745dc"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-6-16","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":6,"verse":16,"english":"Do you dedicate to Yama the lotuses of their faces, severed (in pieces) with your discus. Save you, we have none who can, while tormented with fright, inspire us with courage. Slay in encounter the elated Rākşasas along with their adherents; and even as the sun dried up dew, do you dispel this fear of ours.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.411,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-6-13","DUTT-7-6-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7006016","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6e8d6934916a820a970edc94924a57d159c7c06dc0d067dce9170023138b0e64","compact":"372836c528f7be25aabab0908057b66fb4c5a248777e3bdb37293acc907b8449","nasal":"372836c528f7be25aabab0908057b66fb4c5a248777e3bdb37293acc907b8449"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-6-17","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":6,"verse":17,"english":"Thus accosted by the deities, that god of gods Janārdana who brings fear to foes cheering up the celestial up the celestials, said to them.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-6-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7006017","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8e41ab8bde8ec9f0670d0aa323504bc5eb0f1b4d89160fcb942b38fa2d3fd86a","compact":"b2a7bc56e265def207267a8abe3900423fc6b7a8b54b660b56b6ba742729c4fd","nasal":"b2a7bc56e265def207267a8abe3900423fc6b7a8b54b660b56b6ba742729c4fd"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-6-18","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":6,"verse":18,"english":"'I know the Raksasa, Sukesa, as flushed with the boon bestowed by Iśāna. And I also know his sons, of whom Mālyavān is the eldest. Those worst if Rākṣasas that have over-riden your dignity will I, wrought up with wrath, slay (in battle); therefore, you gods, be of good cheer.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-6-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7006018","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"102c01ecda546d1220d8dcf64ecb1215a25bdc9a7fd55b970729534e1495afc0","compact":"8f0b742679807d1a3d70c908ef8dacd6d6bc8bbac596bdf52ef59808b2d55c45","nasal":"8575331648a5049306ae174afda5e5bae2bae490674367736e87e58a3888bc0f"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-6-19","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":6,"verse":19,"english":"'I know the Raksasa, Sukesa, as flushed with the boon bestowed by Iśāna. And I also know his sons, of whom Mālyavān is the eldest. Those worst if Rākṣasas that have over-riden your dignity will I, wrought up with wrath, slay (in battle); therefore, you gods, be of good cheer.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.5,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-6-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7006019","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f42442ac9b3bd8b9d7656fed81957e0bc4e53a4a1910009edc692cbde6e65c14","compact":"b9b5b0467410841e01760010537370e956d139b860dd02043730899aa1378d58","nasal":"d48217ab6be3901af2162e264f8a4175d8f839600d0e7acb0300a33583d0d74