"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7006025","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f2f300ce9fd21fb2209b617cb8aad595ed885e6cd9288afbebed62b2d419ff74","compact":"d1166a4ea67f299d4e8650e9b30d3cb03d1e086acbe07a3d4919724b040710f2","nasal":"d1166a4ea67f299d4e8650e9b30d3cb03d1e086acbe07a3d4919724b040710f2"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-6-26","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":6,"verse":26,"english":"Thus addressed by the deities, the slayer of Andhaka, hearing their speech, said, shaking his head and hands.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-6-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7006026","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"aa075c3f589c379646308a3a5afba77a0197d82c75735ec767f8cffe962967cf","compact":"f0c8339c47f28f9f3bfed77943b4039a7bb4215902675050574d4e69efc372cd","nasal":"9948812b643169ae33af477245b6c45c9bcba99b7ec9dea51b4b3e26aaa0fc45"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-6-27","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":6,"verse":27,"english":"You gods, Sukesa's sons are incapable of being slain by me in battle. But I shall tell you the means whereby they may be slain.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.767,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-6-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7006027","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4f743a744a901e59b01b1ba238d93a6ff47898175ef50a55170fee8bfd35fc30","compact":"2b03e5e4e4f5d2f08b0adb61bae58b4fbbb77f64240ae1354f13ba24bd29d187","nasal":"cd0c6680a90af2a987e278484d1fe7ee31f8ac920c93918ef62761d94ccbf18b"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-6-28","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":6,"verse":28,"english":"Do you seek the shelter of him who hold the discus and mace in his hands, and who is clad in a yellow attire, of Janardana, Hari, even of the auspicious Nārāyaṇa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.5,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-6-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7006028","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"689c1542d2b09d035f4934d10afb8dcba3d648e2f6d5b2e45f71b94845112dd6","compact":"ee44b240ce67e93a5e0308447d457e062ea0d0ba40cf26580c360fe25584161c","nasal":"ee44b240ce67e93a5e0308447d457e062ea0d0ba40cf26580c360fe25584161c"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-6-29","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":6,"verse":29,"english":"Having received this counsel of Hara, they, rendering reverence to that enemy of Kāma, came the abode of Nārāyana and communicated everything to him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.554,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-6-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7006029","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6327e535cb4b84bfc9c7021880fa5dc2ece004160ca1272e04e33e84e8225c31","compact":"13722b4564465619176299694eb65f51b8bbc3aedfed3bb2e0d13e161bf515ca","nasal":"d69c86e23a510aa66196bd2dbdaed4893c138ed45fea8dc59227bff399531e2d"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-6-30","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":6,"verse":30,"english":"Then Nārāyana spoke to the celestials with Indra at their head, I will slay those foes of the celestials. You gods, cast off all fear!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.656,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-6-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7006030","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d4155c77c274f44f78d8783eb6a2933cdd7e969ad72789ea5fa74ffdd0c0ef33","compact":"0765fc505370d96b66d1e916362a07d556918645010b0018648634d24f23f485","nasal":"da54b4c95ca41c187c501b6298e712291df7da7494781e9928368959faaa7694"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-6-31","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":6,"verse":31,"english":"to O foremost of Rākşasas, Hari promised to the frightened celestials that he would slay us. Therefore do you think as to what is fit.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.703,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-6-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7006031","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ad7ba234543a3ffd00556d229f88499f358a0a3829497f7987afa39bb07d84a8","compact":"7f11c0ffc7e24dd1c121fab5c8f473a42c643771c524a14c0ae11f9e3478c6f6","nasal":"b667b108373d3ed7593f4e4a927d38d0ec20f038924242b9c4bbc6331b293af4"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-6-32","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":6,"verse":32,"english":"Hiranyakaśipu has met with death (at the hands of Hari), as also other enemies of the immortals. And Namuci and Kālanemi, and that foremost of heroes, Sanhrada and Rādheya, and Bahumāyī, and the virtuous Lokapāla, and Yamala, and Arjuna, and Hardikya, and Sumbha and Niśumbhaka, Asuras and Dānavas endowed with strength and possessed of terrific prowess all these, who having come to the field, had never been heard of as worsted, who had performed hundreds of sacrifices, who had been well skilled in illusion, who had been versed in every branch of knowledge, and who were the terrors of their foes have by hundreds and by thousands been destroyed by Narayana. Learning this, it behove you to do what would conduce to the behoof of all. It is a sore task to defeat Narayana, who wish to slay us.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.788,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-6-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7006032","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ba5f975176511c2f0e3b11acf2d2873f7fdeec0266970cf634694bea71f2ad81","compact":"a69024a3e0ecda79a92a1880b67c998502f170dcee7a63de1309b611e3d81631","nasal":"0125d0bf362a8f2479c84b659a3ef4846ccec4d6701648eedd6d224f3fa00ae9"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-6-33","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":6,"verse":33,"english":"Thereat Sumāli and Māli, hearing the words of Malyavān, said to their eldest brother, like the Asvins addressing Vāsava.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.79,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-6-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7006033","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d8d196fdbff9245781c23e4c1f283689bf67e0ef711b4ab23efaea38260a4de4","compact":"a496255bb7af2587a465015e88f0fc7177ca721d5fae278db83f564d5595cee9","nasal":"a496255bb7af2587a465015e88f0fc7177ca721d5fae278db83f564d5595cee9"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-6-34","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":6,"verse":34,"english":"We have studied, performed sacrifices, practised charity, and obtained riches; and attaining long health and long life, we have established sterling righteousness in our path.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.797,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-6-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7006034","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8f587ffc4c3689479bbe3f2ce4d4d3b721c0456d5fd2cd55fa43fad12b5985ec","compact":"292d861b69b77aadafb6d9554bff754ba87c4de65e40c8dcd1e2fa2ed435e825","nasal":"292d861b69b77aadafb6d9554bff754ba87c4de65e40c8dcd1e2fa2ed435e825"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-6-35","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":6,"verse":35,"english":"With arms plunging into the sea of celestials, we have conquered our unrivalled enemies. Therefore, we have no fear touching death.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.438,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-6-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7006035","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7110beb343f676953510df1d2672fbefe1ae6e2252af204abdcc43086ab1d7ad","compact":"86b2d05c15a4c9845049ce02cdb72edb943e777